# Test: a plugin restarted with a changed command module is refused, and its changed commands never reach the daemon
#
# Question: when an external plugin that brought a command module is started
# again and declares that module with another argument bound, does the daemon
# refuse that start under doctor-plugin-schema-changed, naming the command
# module, and does no command of the changed module ever serve a line?
# Why not a unit test: TestStage1RefusesChangedModuleSet proves the comparison
# and that the published set is not written. This proves, on a real daemon
# with a real second process, that the refusal is the operator's warning and
# that the changed bound never judges a typed line.
#
# The fixture's commands-redeclare variant
# (internal/test/fixture/plugin_fixture_external_yang.go) brings the config,
# command and rpc modules on its first start and exits once the daemon is
# ready; its second start brings the command module with the target name cut
# from 1..16 to 1..8 characters (externalyang.CommandsNarrowed). It declares
# failure policy restart, so the daemon starts it again with no operator
# action.
#
# What the daemon does after the refusal, read at the producer: a failed
# restart leaves the plugin down and is not retried (Server.restartPluginWithin
# records StopRestartFailed, internal/component/plugin/server/reload_tx.go).
# The first generation's commands were released before the second one's
# handshake (releasePluginRegistrations, called from restartPluginProcess),
# and the refused second generation registered none, so the dispatcher holds
# no command under `show acme-monitor` and answers "unknown command" for any
# argument (Dispatcher.dispatchPlugin): the argument check of
# Dispatcher.routeToProcessWithEvents is reached only through a registered
# command. Had the changed module been taken, a 12-character name would be
# refused naming 1..8, which the last step rejects.
#
# Steps:
#   1. ze start; the daemon's stderr shows the first start exiting and the
#      second refused, naming acme-monitor-cmd; no second start is ready.
#   2. await the warning doctor-plugin-schema-changed through the daemon's own
#      answer (the barrier, as external-yang-changed-keeps-config.ci does).
#   3. the warning names the command module and says its text is not the one
#      the plugin declared when ze started.
#   4. a 12-character name, which the 1..8 bound would refuse, answers
#      "unknown command" and never names 1..8.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-35 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup.
# PREVENTS: a restarted plugin changing the command model of a running ze, or
#   its refusal naming no module.

option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
bus {
	endpoint acme-monitor {
		external {
			run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang commands-redeclare";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}

acme-monitor {
	target probe-a
	interval 5
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
expect=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang generation 1 is exiting
expect=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang generation 2 was refused
expect=stderr:contains=doctor-plugin-schema-changed
expect=stderr:contains=acme-monitor-cmd
reject=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang generation 2 ready
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL

# The barrier: the daemon's own answer carries the warning the refused second
# start raises. It retries a refused connection, so it also holds the SSH
# listener.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture daemon/await-answer doctor-plugin-schema-changed "show warnings | json":exit=0

# The warning names the command module and the reason.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "show warnings | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=acme-monitor-cmd
expect=stdout:contains=is not the text the plugin declared when ze started

# The changed bound never judges a line: no command of the refused module is
# registered, so the daemon answers as for a path nothing serves.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "show acme-monitor target twelve-chars":exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown command
reject=stderr:contains=1..8
